# Adjustfile — Enaction Engine drift tolerances

@abstract:
Advisory drift checks for documentation evidence, proving-ground provenance,
external identity, and workspace scope.
@end

## Documentation drift

### claim-evidence-alignment
- description: Major README claims retain an EXPLAINME evidence entry
- tolerance: Every implemented claim names an artifact, gate, proof limit, game status, and provenance
- corrective: Narrow the README claim or extend EXPLAINME with real evidence
- severity: advisory

### implementation-status
- description: Target architecture remains visibly distinct from implemented inventory
- tolerance: No future subsystem is described as shipped without code and tests
- corrective: Move unsupported claims back to intended direction
- severity: advisory

## Proving-ground drift

### provenance
- description: Extracted, derived, and new code are not conflated
- tolerance: IDApTIK service is recorded for interpolation; FixedStep remains new until integrated
- corrective: Update claim wording from observed integration evidence
- severity: advisory

### second-game-generality
- description: One-game boundaries remain provisional until challenged by Chronicles of Slavia
- tolerance: No untested boundary is called universally game-neutral
- corrective: Mark the boundary provisional or add second-game evidence
- severity: advisory

## Identity and structure drift

### namespace
- description: New crates, if earned, use the enaction-* namespace
- tolerance: Zero off-namespace workspace packages
- corrective: Rename before publication and update Cargo metadata, imports, docs, and tests
- severity: advisory

### external-providers
- description: GitHub, SonarCloud, and indexed badges converge on canonical identity
- tolerance: Unfinished provider actions are recorded in docs/status/EXTERNAL-ACTIONS.adoc
- corrective: Complete authenticated provider rename, verify targets, then add badges
- severity: advisory
